<title>BAHRAIN: ISLAMIC BANKS LEND MALAYSIA AIRLINE $50 MLN.</title>
<headline>ISLAMIC BANKS LEND MALAYSIA AIRLINE $50 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Jeddah-based Islamic Development Bank (IDB) said on Tuesday it had approved a $50 million financing facility to Malaysian Airline System Bhd (MAS).</p>
<p>IDB said the facility would be extended by the Islamic Banks' Portfolio, which was set up by the IDB and 20 Islamic financial institutions in 1987 to promote trade between Moslem states.</p>
<p>It said the $50 million financing facility was part of $300 million Malaysian Airlines was seeking from international banks. It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
